'' The libclang probe parses a freestanding header for every target and reports clang's
'' layouts -- including the two places the targets disagree. A bit-field's storage unit:
'' Windows starts a new one for 'unsigned char next' after 'unsigned int' bit-fields
'' (bit 32, size 8), SysV packs it into the same one (bit 8, size 4). And an enum of
'' positive values: 'int' under msvc, 'unsigned int' under the gnu triples.
''
'' It is also the ABI test for tiko's own libclang binding: every call below passes or
'' returns a CXCursor, CXType, CXString or CXSourceLocation by value, and the visitor
'' receives cursors by value. build/bootstrap.sh's stage 2 must print the same bytes.
'' TEST: cli
'' HOSTS[macos-arm64]: windows macos
''     (with no macOS SDK, a Linux host's own /usr/include answers the probe)
'' ARGS: --cimport-probe tests/cimport/src/probe.h
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: diag 3
'' EXPECT-NOT: diag 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: struct probe_pair : struct probe_pair size 24 align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field tag : int32_t @bit 0 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field value : double @bit 64 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field name : const char * @bit 128 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field low : unsigned int @bit 0 width 3
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field high : unsigned int @bit 3 width 5
'' EXPECT-OUT: union probe_word : union probe_word size 4 align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT:     field b : unsigned char[4] @bit 0 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT:     const PROBE_BLUE = 40
'' EXPECT-OUT: struct probe_opaque : struct probe_opaque (opaque)
'' EXPECT-OUT: typedef probe_size : probe_size
'' EXPECT-OUT: function probe_add : int (int, int) args 2 variadic 0 cc 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: function probe_printf : int (const char *, ...) args 1 variadic 1 cc 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: function probe_walk : void (struct probe_pair, probe_opaque *) args 2 variadic 0 cc 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: var probe_counter : long
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: target   x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: struct probe_bits : struct probe_bits size 8 align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]:     field next : unsigned char @bit 32 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: underlying int
'' EXPECT-OUT[win64]: target   x86_64-w64-windows-gnu
'' EXPECT-OUT[win64]: struct probe_bits : struct probe_bits size 8 align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT[win64]:     field next : unsigned char @bit 32 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT[win64]: underlying unsigned int
'' EXPECT-OUT[linux-x86_64]: target   x86_64-pc-linux-gnu
'' EXPECT-OUT[linux-x86_64]: struct probe_bits : struct probe_bits size 4 align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT[linux-x86_64]:     field next : unsigned char @bit 8 width -
'' EXPECT-OUT[linux-x86_64]: underlying unsigned int
